    "product_id": "57460398-0cdd-47b6-9671-d6438934f693",
    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 080538\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n1038 PM PDT Mon Sep 7 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Drier conditions expected much of the week with a warming trend. \n\n* Elevated south-southwesterly wind gusts expected across the\n  region in the late week with slight chances for storms on \n  higher terrain.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...Today through Sunday\n\nThe building cloud cover and lingering humidity will help make this \nafternoon be the coolest of the forecast with the upper 80s to mid \n90s expected for most of the valley. The upper level pattern will \nfocus moisture farther to the east into the work week, leading to \ndrying conditions and allowing temperatures to increase as pressure \nbuilds. As of the current forecast, temperatures look to peak on \nThursday with highs around 105 degrees for most of the valley, and \nlooking to exceed 110 degrees in favored warmer areas. Overnight \ntemperatures will also climb over the next few days, peaking in the \nmid 80s to low 90s. These warming temperatures will increase \nHeatRisk, with Major HeatRisk expected in the desert valleys for \nThursday. A pattern shift in the late week will offer a quick \ncooling trend, bringing temperatures to near average over the \nweekend.\n\nThis late week pattern change will also increase winds aross the \nCWA. A trough builds to the north-northwest, and approaches the high \npressure to our east. This will lead to a stronger pressure gradient \nand funnel winds between the two pressure systems, offering stronger \nsouth to southwest winds across the CWA. Widespread winds above 20 \nmph with gusts above 30 mph will be possible Friday afternoon, with \nthe potential for infrequent gusts around 40 mph. Saturday and \nSunday's afternoons call for slightly stronger winds and gusts than \nFriday, with most areas seeing peak winds on Saturday and some \neasing on Sunday. Longer-term models are in fair agreement over \nthese winds, and also that winds ease into the next work week.\n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 06Z Forecast Package...Winds\nwill follow typical daily directional patterns through the \nforecast period, veering to the northeast by mid- to late morning,\nthen gradually to the southeast and southwest by late afternoon. \nWind speeds are expected to remain under 10KT, with VFR conditions\nprevailing. Temperatures Tuesday will remain just under 100 \ndegrees.\n\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast\nCalifornia...For the 06Z Forecast Package...Winds will follow\ntypical daily directional patterns over the next 24 hours, with \nspeeds around 5-10KT. VFR conditions will prevail, with passing \nbands of clouds with bases at or above 12kft.\n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Murdock\nAVIATION...Phillipson\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
